        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The tapestry belongs to a series of hangings showing incidents in the life of an oriental monarch. It is a fanciful European representation of the Emperor of China, K'ang Xi who reigned from 1661-1721, seated on a luxurious carpet-covered chaise, in a procession."@en ;
